  "verbalization": "Acebutolol, through its side effect of Intermittent Claudication, is linked to two other drugs, Celiprolol and Trandolapril, both of which are indicated for hypertension. This suggests a potential mechanistic pathway where the side effect of Acebutolol may influence the therapeutic use of these medications in the context of hypertension. The evidence is supported by the presence of overlapping side effects and indications, indicating a possible role of Acebutolol in the pathophysiology of hypertension through its effects on the cardiovascular system. The final scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further investigation is needed to confirm the direct mechanistic link. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of considering side effects and their associated indications in the re-evaluation of drug use for hypertension.",
